{
  "candidate_rtl": "module mul_subexpression(
    input [7:0] multiplicand,  // 8-bit multiplicand
    input [7:0] multiplier,    // 8-bit multiplier
    output [15:0] product      // 16-bit product output
);

// Generate all partial products, keeping original indexing/commutation.
wire [7:0] pp [0:7];
genvar i, j;
generate
    for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin: gen_rows
        for (j = 0; j < 8; j = j + 1) begin: gen_cols
            assign pp[i][j] = multiplicand[i] & multiplier[j];
        end
    end
endgenerate

// Shift each partial-product row.
wire [15:0] p [0:7];
generate
    for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin: gen_shift
        assign p[i] = {8'b0, pp[i]} << i;
    end
endgenerate

// Balanced binary reduction tree: depth 3 instead of serial depth 7.
wire [15:0] s01, s23, s45, s67;
wire [15:0] s0123, s4567;

assign s01 = p[0] + p[1];
assign s23 = p[2] + p[3];
assign s45 = p[4] + p[5];
assign s67 = p[6] + p[7];

assign s0123 = s01 + s23;
assign s4567 = s45 + s67;

assign product = s0123 + s4567;

endmodule",
  "bottleneck": "The original RTL accumulates the eight shifted partial-product rows serially: sum[i] = sum[i-1] + shifted_partial. This creates a dependency chain of seven carry-propagate additions. Even after synthesis optimization, this serial accumulate pattern tends to dominate the mapped-cell maximum data arrival because each addition must wait for the previous result, forming a deep logic path.",
  "rewrite": "Keep the same partial-product generation but replace the serial accumulation with a balanced binary tree of additions. The eight shifted partial products are first added in pairs (p0+p1, p2+p3, p4+p5, p6+p7), then those sums are combined in pairs, and finally the top two sums are added. This preserves the exact same set of adders (seven) but reduces the logic depth from seven serial adders to three balanced levels, exposing parallelism and allowing synthesis to exploit faster carry-lookahead or other optimized adder structures.",
  "expected_timing_gain": "Estimated roughly 2x reduction in maximum data arrival (from ~7 serial adder levels to ~3 balanced levels). Actual mapped timing improvement must be confirmed by EDA, but the logic-depth reduction is expected to significantly shorten the critical path.",
  "area_or_other_cost": "Area is expected to remain close to baseline because the total number of adders is unchanged (seven); only their organization changes. Some minor wiring or signal-sharing differences may occur, but the design should stay well within the +10% area cap (3261.878 um^2 vs baseline 2965.344 um^2).",
  "functional_boundaries": "Preserves the exact module name `mul_subexpression`, input/output ports, widths, unsigned full-product behavior, and all 256x256 input combinations. No clocks, state, input restrictions, assumptions, or don't-cares are introduced."
}
